- H-c2: the scale is confirmed and the stage identified. In the falling inputs the selection
  stage carries the whole loss (noise stages within ±0.01 of their expectations), and the loss is
  sym3 (the sign-symmetric background term). But the coefficient is NOT constant from t = 10: it
  grows from −0.01..−0.03 (0..9) to −0.02..−0.05 (10..24), −0.03..−0.07 (25..49) and −0.07..−0.18
  (50..99), 3–5× over 10..100: a coupling that builds up with time under the move, as H-link
  predicts (the association has to accumulate), and as a constant b²V_G coefficient does not.

